module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_alias_operand_in_equality_is_admitted_without_judging_its_expansion

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CeilingNotStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data an_alias_operand_in_equality_is_admitted_without_judging_its_expansion: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_alias_operand_in_equality_is_admitted_without_judging_its_expansion" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingNotStated },

  receipts: [
    "**An `==` whose operands are typed by a type ALIAS compiles with zero diagnostics and emits a plain `==`, although the alias expands to a declaration with a function-valued member**, so the equality plan never judges the members of the expansion.",

    "**SPECIMEN, measured (gunbc#15175, srdk26 on srv2, gunbc 115320ca1171 built from the patched tree at fixed point, 2026-11-03):** five one-file compiles each returned rc 0 with 0 diagnostics and emitted no equality_derived function. a4: `type Al = Cell` with `type Cell fn-valued member` compared directly (no generic, no applied argument). a3: an alias of a generic declared in the SAME module over a function-valued cell. a1: an alias of an IMPORTED generic over a function-valued cell. a5: a holder record whose member is the alias. a2 (plain cell) is the control and is admitted correctly. Not cargo-checked.",

    "**Distinct from the imported-generic peel** (a reference to an imported generic applied to a function-valued argument, repaired in gunbc#15175 by keeping the peeled applied arguments across re-entry in equality_leaf_walk): a4 has no generic and no arguments to drop, and a3 is same-module, so the applied-arguments rule cannot reach it. The base compiler at e0ac4728caa0 also fails the a1-shaped claim; the base was not measured on a2-a5.",

    "**INFERRED, NOT MEASURED:** expand_nominal_alias_rhs returns the expansion through with_authored_identity, so the expansion carries the ALIAS identity; the equality leaf walk then reads resolved identity equal to the reference identity and treats the alias as the declaration itself, which would route it past the members judgement. No instrument has located the branch.",

    "**RUNG: BELOW CEILING, unread.** The class is decidable and fully modeled (the equality plan already judges declarations), so its ceiling is a refused program; today the wrong answer is a silently admitted `==`.",

    "**Next-rung trigger, a capability:** the equality walk judges an alias by the declaration identity of its expansion. The expecting-red controls a1 and a4 (admitted today, must refuse with EqualityOnFunctionMember or EqualityMemberUnjudgeable) belong with the follow-up lane, not gunbc#15175.",

    "**Recognition rule:** wherever a walk compares an expansion identity against the reference identity to decide whether it has left the reference, ask whether an alias expansion is made to carry the reference identity.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
